From 136e05543c0c1dd39b1eb15ef9eb93002e675c1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:46:45 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] video-driver: iris33: look up power resources by platform

The iris33 power sequences name their clocks, power domains and resets
with the vendor device tree names (gcc_video_axi0_clk, iris-ctl,
video_xo_reset, ...), and the resource helpers match those names
against the platform tables, which follow the clock-names,
power-domain-names and reset-names of the device tree. A platform
probed from an upstream qcom-iris device tree names the same resources
iface, core, vcodec0_core, venus, vcodec0, bus, core and xo, so the
iris33 sequences cannot drive it: clock lookups fail, and gdsc_on
silently skips a domain it does not find.

Collect the names in one table that the power sequences and the clock
scaling code read, selected by the variant init function, with the
vendor names as the only entry for now. Allow the MVS0 reset to be
absent, as the upstream binding has none. No functional change for the
existing iris33 platforms.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending [qualcomm-linux/video-driver]
